![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

These security headers are a great addition. Here are a couple of suggestions to align them with the latest best practices:

1.  **`X-XSS-Protection`**: This header is deprecated and can introduce vulnerabilities in older browsers. It's recommended to disable the browser's XSS auditor by setting it to `0`.
2.  **`Permissions-Policy`**: Consider adding this header to enhance privacy by disabling features like Google's FLoC (`interest-cohort`).

Applying these changes will further harden the application's security posture.

```suggestion
        add_header X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN" always;
        add_header X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff" always;
        add_header X-XSS-Protection "0" always;
        add_header Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin" always;
        add_header Permissions-Policy "interest-cohort=()" always;
```
